        model: "The Chief Experience Officer owns the intelligent UX principles: what may be suggested, how it is explained and how it can be switched off. The data protection officer may veto any use of data and must agree before a new personalisation goes live; the doctors check every suggestion about health content; the innovation team proposes and pilots. A new intelligent function needs a short record: what it suggests, from which data, how it explains itself, how it is switched off. When innovation and trust conflict, trust and data protection come first, then the member's benefit, then economics; the management decides what that does not settle.",
